text:
Written for The Evening Star by Charles


Stevenson.


To strive with happy heart for something good,
The while feels a tenderness for those


Whom fate has burdened with increasing woesj
To hope that what is darkly understood
VIII blossom white, as blooms the barren wood;
To feel a love that like the bestows


Life giving cheer thorn-tree rose;
To quickly do what conscience says one should;
Pause not, fail not, continue to the end;


These constitute zeal, which, like a song,
Bears the rapt soul above the reach Of wrong;
And teaches how they help who willing bend
Their lofty aspirations low to aid


Some human need selfish world has made.

